# Devon EC2 RDP — FULL environment template (Devon ONLY).
# Copy to `.env` in the repo root on the EC2 RDP host, then fill in
# ONLY the keys you use, via secure entry on that machine.
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY in this file. NEVER real tokens/keys/secrets here,
# NEVER in chat, NEVER in screenshots, NEVER in git. `.env` is gitignored.
# Devon boots fully offline against the Mock provider with no keys set.
#
# DEVON HAS TWO TELEGRAM BOTS (both Devon, both in this file):
#   1. DEVON MAIN bot  - NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN         - GATED (stays gated)
#   2. SECOND DEVON bot - NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_PERSONAL_BOT_TOKEN - USER-ONLY (owner only)
# Separate tokens, separate getUpdates pollers. NEVER share one token
# across two bots (two pollers on one token = missed commands / 409).
# There is NO other bot in Devon's config. Any other trading bot
# lives in its own repo with its own config and is NOT part of Devon.
#
# HOW TO FILL: on the EC2 RDP, open PowerShell, run `notepad .env`,
# paste values from your secure store. Or use the Secure Vault flow.
# REQUIRED on EC2: one LLM key (Groq recommended) + both Devon bot tokens.
# OPTIONAL: everything else - leave blank/commented if unused.
# API-FIRST (owner decision): NO GGUF, NO local LLM, NO llama.cpp, NO Ollama.
# LLM / STT / TTS / diffusion all via API keys below, till better hosting.
# Singing = generation to audio FILES (EC2 has no speaker). Files are
# sent via Telegram / saved to disk. Same voice/music stack, file output.

# ══ REQUIRED — DEVON TELEGRAM BOTS (2) ══

# ── 1. DEVON MAIN BOT — GATED (stays gated) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 = Devon main bot polls getUpdates. Must be 1 on EC2.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_BOT_ENABLED=
# REQUIRED for bot 1. DEVON MAIN bot token (GATED - stays gated). From @BotFather. NEVER paste in chat. Separate token from bot 2; never share one token across two pollers.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Chat IDs the main (gated) bot serves. Comma-separated.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_BOT_CHATS=
# 0 for the main bot (no owner-private relationship context in gated chats).
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_BOT_PARTNER_CONTEXT=

# ── 2. SECOND DEVON BOT — USER-ONLY (owner only, no one else) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 = second Devon bot polls getUpdates. Must be 1 on EC2.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_PERSONAL_BOT_ENABLED=
# REQUIRED for bot 2. SECOND DEVON bot token (USER-ONLY - owner only, no one else). From @BotFather, DIFFERENT bot from main. NEVER paste in chat.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_PERSONAL_BOT_TOKEN=
# Owner-only chat IDs for the second bot. Comma-separated.
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_PERSONAL_BOT_CHATS=
# 1 for the second bot (owner-only, full context).
# NM_CHAT_TELEGRAM_PERSONAL_BOT_PARTNER_CONTEXT=

